From: hamza <hamza@book4>
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] phy: qcom-qmp: register clocks before enabling runtime PM

CCF snapshots pm_runtime_enabled() when a clock is registered and takes a
provider runtime reference while that clock is prepared. QMP's generated
PIPE clock feeds the GCC gate consumed by the PHY itself. Registering it
after enabling runtime PM creates a self-vote: the prepared PIPE source
keeps the PHY active, but only its suspend callback releases PIPE.

The two Book4 USB-C combo PHY PIPE providers were observed with cached
rpm_enabled=1 and prepare_count=1. The multiport GCC PIPE gates on this
kernel have no parents, so this is not the explanation for the separate
USB-A runtime test failure caused by duplicate DWC3/xHCI PHY ownership.

Register the software clock providers before enabling runtime PM in the
USB, legacy USB, combo and USBC probes. Their fixed-rate/cached DP-rate
operations do not access PHY hardware. Keep runtime PM enabled before
creating the generic PHY devices, and retain the default forbid policy.
No clocks or runtime references are forcibly disabled.

The original registration order fails the regression using extracted CCF
helpers; the correction passes for all four drivers. All four modules
compile (legacy uses a make-only configuration override on this machine).
USB/DisplayPort operation, suspend and power savings remain hardware-untested.
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c      | 10 +++++-----
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-usb-legacy.c |  9 +++++----
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-usb.c        |  9 +++++----
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-usbc.c       |  9 +++++----
 4 files changed, 20 insertions(+), 17 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
index 2ebaa16a1..b94cf2bf3 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -4969,6 +4969,11 @@ static int qmp_combo_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_node_put;
 
+	/* PIPE self-vote prevention: clock registration before runtime PM */
+	ret = qmp_combo_register_clocks(qmp, usb_np, dp_np);
+	if (ret)
+		goto err_node_put;
+
 	/*
 	 * Enable runtime PM support, but forbid it by default.
 	 * Users can allow it again via the power/control attribute in sysfs.
@@ -4979,11 +4984,6 @@ static int qmp_combo_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_node_put;
 
-	ret = qmp_combo_register_clocks(qmp, usb_np, dp_np);
-	if (ret)
-		goto err_node_put;
-
-
 	qmp->usb_phy = devm_phy_create(dev, usb_np, &qmp_combo_usb_phy_ops);
 	if (IS_ERR(qmp->usb_phy)) {
 		ret = PTR_ERR(qmp->usb_phy);
